      "problem": "Let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=\\frac{7}{2}{x}^{2}+3$ defined on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $G(x)=7x$ from the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{2}{x}^{2}+3∼3+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{6}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{14(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}}\nand\n{{field-3}}\non $R,$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n7x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-4}}\\cdot {{field-5}}.\n$$",
